hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15840","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Kill snakes, and kill the one with two stripes and the tail-less, for they cause miscarriage and blind the sight. Ibn Umar said: Abu Lubabah or Zayd ibn al-Khattab saw me chasing a snake to kill it, and he forbade me. I said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded killing them. He said: He forbade after that killing the snakes of houses. al-Zuhri said: They are the dwellers."
"15841","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the minbar saying: Kill the snake, and kill the one with two stripes and the tail-less, for they snatch the sight and cause miscarriage. He said: So I would not see a snake but I killed it. Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir said to me: Will you not open a small door between me and you? I said: Yes. He said: So I stood with him and we opened it, and a snake came out, and I rushed at it to kill it. He said to me: Wait. I said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded killing them. He said: He forbade killing the snakes of houses."
"15842","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me that al-Husayn ibn al-Saib ibn Abi Lubabah informed that Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir, when Allah accepted his repentance, said: O Messenger of Allah, part of my repentance is to abandon the home of my people and reside with you, and to strip myself of my wealth as charity for Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A third suffices you."
"15843","Muhammad narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: From Abd Rabbi, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he used to command killing all snakes. Abu Lubabah asked his permission to enter from a small door of theirs to the mosque, and he saw them killing a snake, so Abu Lubabah said to them: Has it not reached you that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing the snakes of houses and homes, and commanded killing the one with two stripes and the tail-less."
"15844","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubaydillah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he opened a door and a snake came out of it, and he ordered killing it. Abu Lubabah said to him: Do not do it, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing the snakes that are in houses."
